    "description": "<h3 data-local-id=\"3981279f63ae\">Summary</h3><p data-local-id=\"1df488707412\">Signups can already name a Paused or Banned referrer without being blocked — Kobi confirmed this at the 9/24 sync, so the original &quot;flag-don&#039;t-block&quot; automation this ticket was built around isn&#039;t needed. </p><p data-local-id=\"9f56d6ad896b\"><strong>The ticket is rescoped to just surfacing a report or notification for Ops when a signup names a banned/paused referrer, since Emily noted this is a useful signal for investigating referrer networks.</strong></p><h3 data-local-id=\"d8e1cff54038\">Requirements</h3><ul data-local-id=\"0e4fa22d2842\"><li data-local-id=\"576f884d6830\"><p data-local-id=\"ff6e9350474d\">A report or notification surfacing signups where the named referrer&#039;s status is Paused or Banned.</p></li></ul><h3 data-local-id=\"2cf5ff3a78cb\">Constraints</h3><ul data-local-id=\"a6deb3bbc541\"><li data-local-id=\"f91af170e71a\"><p data-local-id=\"47ab11de3c77\">No changes to signup completion behavior — referrer selection and signup completion must continue working exactly as they do now (unblocked).</p></li></ul><h3 data-local-id=\"df59286ca7d3\">Acceptance Criteria</h3><ol data-local-id=\"5147c2301bb3\"><li data-local-id=\"cb6eec4d9388\"><p data-local-id=\"144baacbbdec\">Ops has a way to view signups whose named referrer is currently Paused or Banned.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"18284fcdd3f2\"><p data-local-id=\"022d6612a43c\">Signup completion is unaffected — selecting a paused/banned referrer does not block or alter the signup flow.</p></li></ol><h3 data-local-id=\"877248db685e\">Assumptions</h3><ul data-local-id=\"810d1321938b\"><li data-local-id=\"088b6ae812ee\"><p data-local-id=\"e15e9fd08720\">Referrer status (Paused/Banned) is already a queryable field on the Sign-Up or Referrer record, since no new status logic is in scope here.</p></li></ul><h3 data-local-id=\"f26f112e46aa\">Open Questions</h3><ul data-local-id=\"a25227f8d736\"><li data-local-id=\"88507e72a219\"><p data-local-id=\"2b4c9647f10c\">Reporting mechanism not yet decided — list view, dashboard component, or an alert/notification are all still on the table.</p></li></ul><h3 data-local-id=\"7dcc8a214f1a\">Dependencies</h3><ul data-local-id=\"8589069873a8\"><li data-local-id=\"aeccb489e5c1\"><p data-local-id=\"92fb7f80cd2f\">Referrer status field/model — originally tied to BUILD-185 (Referrer: Object + Core Status).</p></li></ul><h3 data-local-id=\"cc764981cedb\">Out of Scope</h3><ul data-local-id=\"b75a910225e0\"><li data-local-id=\"552cde22f8ba\"><p data-local-id=\"236292560b5b\">The original flag-don&#039;t-block automation (mirrored from PL-9) — descoped, since blocking was never actually happening and no new signup-flow logic is required.</p></li></ul><h3 data-local-id=\"b0272f3e43b3\">References</h3><ul data-local-id=\"b55608b6e13a\"><li data-local-id=\"2a10c4e263a9\"><p data-local-id=\"7bc83cef0ca9\">Wagertech Internal Sync, Sep 24, 2026 (~01:02:29–01:03:48)</p></li><li data-local-id=\"d68221107075\"><p data-local-id=\"1a6f5c1e6a4e\">Original ticket source: RF-11 — Referrer Record User Stories doc</p></li><li data-local-id=\"17744ac0c581\"><p data-local-id=\"716c5ef9e874\">Aug 18 Weekly Sync — Emily Vandenberg, &quot;flag, don&#039;t block&quot; (<a href=\"https://fathom.video/calls/787411922?timestamp=5599\">Fathom, 1:33:19</a>)</p></li></ul>",
